WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.650
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.110
That number is 2 1 9 2.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.170
David P..

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.820
Here's a voicemail about non voters.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.280
Hi, David.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.360
On sixty two and a lifelong voter, I was join
you.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.670
What can I tell friends who have no interest
in voting?

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.830
What do I tell them?

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.730
How do I convince others that they need to
vote?

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.539
This is a whole topic, but my strategy that
I anecdotally believe is the most effective

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:29.460
is to explain to people if you're up.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.989
Out because you don't think your vote makes
a difference, you're actually helping someone

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:35.989
by not voting.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:41.219
Not voting is an active decision and you're
still making the decision by not voting.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:47.039
It just may not be the decision you want to
be making when you opt out.

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:50.499
You are not saying I am.

00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:55.420
You might be thinking that you're saying I
dislike every candidate, so I'm not participating.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.109
But you are still helping one candidate over
another when you choose not to vote.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:03.260
And most importantly, about not voters.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.210
If everybody who had this thought, my vote
doesn't matter.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.960
So I'm going to stay home.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.480
If all of those people didn't stay home as
a group, their votes would now very much matter

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.070
and would be powerful enough to flip elections.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.240
That's what I've found most effective to talk
to nonvoters.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.610
But most importantly, make sure that they
know you're still choosing when you don't

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.200
vote and you might be choosing for the person
you.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.290
You like the least to be actually the one
elected.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.150
I've made some progress with that argument
with with small groups of people.

